This rule applies to every agent once the supervised plugin is connected.

Non-trivial work starts with `/strict-mode`. Read `principles.md` in this plugin, then this repo's `AGENTS.md`. Pick one playbook. Copy its steps into the todo list. Each step ends in a check.

Code that crosses a function boundary waits on a type sketch. See Design in `skills/strict-mode/SKILL.md`.

After the code change: `/no-comments`, then `/deslop`, then Review, then `/verify`. Reply and PR body: `/unslop`. Skill or prompt edits also need `/eval`. The human merges.

Product rules (UI, copy, colors, locale, schema, verify command) come from `AGENTS.md`. Do not invent them.

Code: no narrating comments, no `any`/`as` to silence the compiler, no one-caller wrappers, no try/catch on trusted paths. Match the file you are in.

Secrets stay out of chat and git.

Trivial (typo, question, one-line explain): do not force the playbook.
Opt-out: user says strict-mode is off.
